@page "/datagrid-ai-column"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor DataGrid <strong>AI Column</strong>
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Add a column whose values are generated by an AI model from the data of each row - taglines, categories, sentiment or translations - computed for the visible page in a single request.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="DataGrid" Example="DataGridAIColumn">
    <DataGridAIColumn />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mt-8">
    The column uses a <code>Template</code> that reads from a dictionary keyed by product id. After the first render and on every <code>Page</code> event the page asks the <code>IChatClient</code> from
    <code>IAIChatService.GetChatClient()</code> for the rows of the current page that have no value yet, asking for a JSON object with <code>ChatResponseFormat.Json</code>, so one request covers the whole page. Rows show a <code>RadzenSkeleton</code> until their value arrives.
</RadzenText>
